From 477818756e5bdf7a7dcf7fd225595a948c0082c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code Review <claude-review@example.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:36:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add QR code scan analytics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- prisma: add ScanEvent model (qrLinkId, scannedAt, ipHash, userAgent)
  with an index on (qrLinkId, scannedAt); matching migration included
- src/lib/scanTracking.js: logScan() records a scan without ever
  throwing, so a failed analytics write can't break the actual
  redirect. IPs are hashed (SHA-256), not stored raw — people
  scanning a code aren't app users and haven't agreed to anything
- redirect/[slug].js: logs a scan (awaited, not fire-and-forget,
  since serverless functions can be frozen/killed shortly after the
  response — an un-awaited write could silently be dropped) before
  issuing the redirect
- api/qr/list.js: returns scanCount and lastScannedAt per link, via
  a _count and one grouped query rather than N+1 per-link queries
- QrTable.js: new Scans column showing count + last-scanned date
- privacy.js: disclose scan-event collection, including for people
  without an account who are scanning someone else's code
